  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Use a substitution such as $u=4^x$ to solve each equation. Give each solution as a rational number, or approximate to three decimal places.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2^{4x}-7\\times2^{2x}+12=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ or $x\\approx0.792$.\n\nUse $u=4^x$ to obtain a quadratic.",
          "worked": "Let $u=4^x=2^{2x}>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-7u+12&=0\\\\(u-4)(u-3)&=0\\\\u&=4\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\n\nReturning to $x$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4^x&=4\\text{ or }3\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }\\log_4 3\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }\\frac{\\log_{10}3}{\\log_{10}4}\\\\x&=1\\text{ or approximately }0.792\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$100^x-10^x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx0.209$.\n\nUse $u=10^x$ and retain only the positive quadratic root.",
          "worked": "Let $u=10^x>0$, so $100^x=u^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-u-1&=0\\\\u&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $\\frac{1-\\sqrt5}{2}<0$, since $10^x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10^x&=\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}\\\\x&=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)\\\\x&\\approx0.209\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\frac15\\right)^{2x}-7\\times\\left(\\frac15\\right)^x+10=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$ or $x\\approx-0.431$.\n\nUse $u=\\left(\\frac15\\right)^x$ to obtain a quadratic.",
          "worked": "Let $u=\\left(\\frac15\\right)^x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-7u+10&=0\\\\(u-5)(u-2)&=0\\\\u&=5\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\n\nReturning to $x$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac15\\right)^x&=5\\text{ or }2\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }\\log_{1/5}2\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }\\frac{\\log_{10}2}{\\log_{10}(1/5)}\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or approximately }-0.431\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 86
      }
    ]
  },
